    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d686">

                <pb facs="0735" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1992B</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-19T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 19, 1915, 3 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1968. Your 2586, July 15, 7 p. m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d686-f1"/> Have indicated
                    to you unwillingness of this Government to enter into any <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi>. It is entirely a question of
                    principle which does not admit of compromise, since that would affect the
                    freedom of American citizens to traverse the high seas to which they are
                    entitled as a matter of right. In your conversations with Foreign Office avoid
                    giving hope that your Government might consider any form of compromise.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
